        "\n",
        "# Question 5: Compare and contrast LangChain and LlamaIndex. What unique problems does each solve?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Answer:\n",
        "\n",
        "### Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "LangChain and LlamaIndex are Python frameworks used to build applications powered by Large Language Models (LLMs). Both help developers connect LLMs with external data and create AI applications, but they focus on different areas.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Difference Between LangChain and LlamaIndex\n",
        "\n",
        "| LangChain | LlamaIndex |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| Focuses on building complete LLM applications and workflows. | Focuses on connecting LLMs with external data. |\n",
        "| Provides chains, prompts, agents, tools and memory. | Provides data loading, indexing, retrieval and query engines. |\n",
        "| Helps combine LLMs with APIs, tools and multiple steps. | Helps retrieve relevant information from documents and databases. |\n",
        "| Commonly used for chatbots, AI assistants and tool-based applications. | Commonly used for document-based question answering and RAG systems. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### Unique Problems Solved\n",
        "\n",
        "**1. LangChain**\n",
        "\n",
        "LangChain simplifies the development of applications that require multiple steps or tools. It connects language models with prompts, external APIs, databases and other components.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Example:* A chatbot that receives a question, calls a weather API, and uses an LLM to explain the weather information.\n",
        "\n",
        "**2. LlamaIndex**\n",
        "\n",
        "LlamaIndex simplifies the process of making private or external data accessible to LLMs. It organizes documents into indexes and retrieves relevant information to answer user questions.\n",
        "\n",
        "*Example:* A system that searches company documents and answers questions based on their contents.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Conclusion\n",
        "\n",
        "LangChain is mainly useful for coordinating LLMs, tools and application workflows, while LlamaIndex specializes in data ingestion, indexing and retrieval. Both frameworks can also be combined to build powerful applications such as document-based AI chatbots."
